  "verbalization": "Adomiparin is linked to Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC) through a series of indirect pathways, primarily through the indication of Purpura Fulminans and Ardeparin. The evidence suggests that Adomiparin may be associated with DIC via its role in causing Purpura Fulminans, which in turn is linked to Heparin, Bovine or Ardeparin. This implies a potential mechanism where Adomiparin could contribute to the pathophysiology of DIC through its interaction with coagulation pathways, possibly via anticoagulant or procoagulant effects. The overlapping indications and the shared outcome of DIC highlight a possible role of Adomiparin in the development of coagulopathy, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a relationship between Adomiparin and DIC through a chain of indications, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise biological pathways involved.",
